<title>UK: Assoc British Ports MD to step down.</title>
<headline>Assoc British Ports MD to step down.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The managing director of Associated British Ports, the port operating subsidiary of Associated British Ports Holdings, has decided to step down for personal reasons, the parent company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Alastair Channing will not seek re-election when he retires at the annual meeting in April next year. His successor would be announced &quot;in due course&quot;, the company said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
